=== (2) THE GAP, AS `#883` MEASURED IT AND WITH THE FORMATS MATCHED ===
  homosexuality  3-item index   residual **0.789** (|rho| 0.459)
  abortion       SINGLE binary  residual **0.448** (|rho| 0.743)  ⇒ Δ as `#883` measured it = **+0.342**
  abortion       3-item index   residual **0.738** (|rho| 0.512)  ⇒ **Δ_matched = +0.051**

=== (3) THE ATTENUATION-ONLY NULL — kind of null NAMED, and it is the whole rival ===
  two item-pairs simulated with ONE shared true coupling and EACH SIDE'S MEASURED reliability; whatever Δ it produces is what measurement error explains for free.
  shared true |rho| 0.486 · rel(homo sanction) 0.802 · rel(abortion trio) 0.789
  attenuation-only Δ: median **-0.003** · 95th **+0.030**
  observed Δ_matched **+0.051** ⇒ above what attenuation alone explains: **True**

=== (4) PAIRED BOOTSTRAP ON Δ_matched — same people, so resample PEOPLE ===
  Δ_matched +0.051  95% [+0.013,+0.088]  excludes 0: **True**

=== (5) THE DISATTENUATION BOUND — the norm reliabilities are NOT identified, so solve ===
  at what homosexuality-NORM reliability would the gap vanish, holding everything else?
  abortion NORM 2-item Spearman-Brown reliability (`abpoorw`+`abdefctw`, n=1813): **0.761**
  the homosexuality norm would need reliability **<= 0.79**
  ⇒ attenuation-explains-it requires the homosexuality norm to be far less reliable than the abortion norm: **False**

=== (6) POSITIVE CONTROL — add noise to the abortion sanction, floor and ceiling MEASURED ===
  g=0.00  abortion residual = 0.738
  g=0.10  abortion residual = 0.801
  g=0.25  abortion residual = 0.909
  g=0.50  abortion residual = 0.956
  g=0.80  abortion residual = 0.989
  measured FLOOR 0.738 · CEILING 0.989 ⇒ the homosexuality residual (0.789) lies strictly between them: True
  => positive control **PASS** — noise raises the residual monotonically, and **at g=0 the abortion residual is 0.738, nowhere near homosexuality's 0.789**

=== (7) NEGATIVE CONTROL — a global permutation. This zero SHOULD be zero ===
  null mean -0.0008 · |null| 95th 0.0425 -> **PASS**

=== (8) SPECIFICATION CURVE + MULTIPLICITY — all 35 trios, whole grid ===
